# Cairn live ISO package list — installed into the live environment only.
# (The *target* system's list is installer/packages/target-packages.x86_64.)
#
# Forked from archiso's releng profile. Last synced with archiso 90:
#   /usr/share/archiso/configs/releng/packages.x86_64
#
# Re-sync after an archiso upgrade, then update the version above:
#   diff <(sed '/^[[:blank:]]*#/d;/^[[:blank:]]*$/d' profile/packages.x86_64) \
#        <(sort /usr/share/archiso/configs/releng/packages.x86_64)
#
# Deltas from releng 90 — added by Cairn, keep these across a re-sync:
#   cage, foot, ttf-jetbrains-mono, ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols-mono
#     The installer's session. The kernel virtual console has sixteen colours
#     and a font format that tops out at 512 bitmap glyphs, so a Nerd Font
#     cannot be loaded onto it at all. cage (a Wayland kiosk) running foot (a
#     truecolor terminal) gives the installer real colour and real icons;
#     /usr/local/bin/cairn-session starts it and falls back to the bare
#     console, where the installer switches to an ASCII glyph set.
#
#     The font is split deliberately: ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd is the same
#     typeface with the icons already patched in, but it installs 232 MiB of
#     every weight and style. The plain face plus the symbols-only font is
#     ~10 MiB for the identical result, with foot listing the symbols font as
#     the fallback. The *target* system still gets the patched font — that is a
#     desktop, not a live image.
# When Cairn intentionally adds or drops a package, list it here with the
# reason so the next re-sync doesn't silently undo the decision.
#
# Historical note: broadcom-wl was dropped (from releng too) when it left the
# official repos; only broadcom-wl-dkms remains, which would need dkms +
# linux-headers in the ISO. airootfs/etc/modprobe.d/broadcom-wl.conf stays,
# matching releng.
#
# mkarchiso strips '#' comments and blank lines from this file before pacstrap.

